WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.175 --> 00:00:08.894
Diego Alvarez: Hey Brittany, hey Frank. Thanks for carving out time this afternoon. How's the week going over there?

2
00:00:10.316 --> 00:00:19.989
Brittany Sawyer: Busy. We had two BDC folks out with the flu Monday and Tuesday, so I was on the phones myself half the week.

3
00:00:19.989 --> 00:00:25.876
Brittany Sawyer: Volume's actually up, we crossed about 2,300 calls last month across the seven stores.

4
00:00:27.123 --> 00:00:31.751
Frank DeLuca: Which is good and bad. Good for the pipeline, bad for Brittany's voicemail inbox.

5
00:00:32.743 --> 00:00:43.590
Brittany Sawyer: Ha, yeah. But the tracking side is fine, calls are landing on the right campaigns and the Google Ads conversions are flowing the way they should.

6
00:00:44.736 --> 00:00:50.948
Diego Alvarez: That's good to hear. Anything on the Salesforce side you want me to look at while we're on?

7
00:00:52.317 --> 00:01:00.006
Brittany Sawyer: No, that's working. Records are writing over fine, the BDC reps don't complain about it, which is basically a compliment.

8
00:01:00.257 --> 00:01:08.940
Diego Alvarez: I'll take it. So I wanted to spend most of this on the renewal, since we're a couple months out. What's the temperature on your side?

9
00:01:09.587 --> 00:01:33.281
Frank DeLuca: I'll jump in. I came over in August, so this is my first pass at the contract. When I sat down with our controller, she went through this year's invoice against last year's line by line and the thing that jumped out was all the separate line items on top of the base platform.

10
00:01:33.521 --> 00:01:36.316
Diego Alvarez: Okay. Which ones stood out to her?

11
00:01:37.648 --> 00:01:46.638
Frank DeLuca: PreSense is billed on its own, the quality management seats are billed on their own, the AI Voice Agent is metered by the minute.

12
00:01:46.638 --> 00:01:54.880
Frank DeLuca: She asked me why we're paying four times for one phone call, and honestly I didn't have a clean answer for her.

13
00:01:56.188 --> 00:02:06.148
Diego Alvarez: That's fair. I can't restructure line items from this call, but I want to get the details right. Can you send me the invoice she was working from?

14
00:02:06.908 --> 00:02:15.505
Frank DeLuca: I can. And I'll be straight with you, while she was doing that comparison she was also taking a call from Marchex.

15
00:02:15.505 --> 00:02:23.712
Frank DeLuca: They came in under what we're paying now on a per-rooftop basis, and they were throwing call scoring into the number.

16
00:02:24.092 --> 00:02:26.572
Diego Alvarez: Per rooftop meaning per store per month?

17
00:02:27.325 --> 00:02:36.316
Frank DeLuca: Per store, flat, all seven of ours. And I've now had two conversations with a dealer group down in Oklahoma City that already made the switch.

18
00:02:36.316 --> 00:02:40.466
Frank DeLuca: So it's not just a cold pitch anymore, it's people I know.

19
00:02:41.824 --> 00:02:44.712
Diego Alvarez: Understood. What are they telling you about it?

20
00:02:45.688 --> 00:02:54.275
Frank DeLuca: Mostly that the math was simpler. I don't have a strong feeling about the product itself, that's not what's driving it.

21
00:02:54.275 --> 00:02:55.501
Frank DeLuca: It's the paperwork.

22
00:02:55.987 --> 00:03:00.812
Diego Alvarez: Got it. And Brittany, is this the same conversation you're getting?

23
00:03:02.096 --> 00:03:15.585
Brittany Sawyer: From my side it's procurement. Every time something new gets added, it's a separate approval with a separate justification, and by the time we get to renewal it feels like we're re-buying the platform three more times.

24
00:03:15.585 --> 00:03:28.344
Brittany Sawyer: If that doesn't get easier, I can't promise we're not looking at what else is out there before January. I'm not saying we're leaving, but I'd be doing my job wrong if I didn't look.

25
00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:47.708
Diego Alvarez: No, I'd rather know now than in December. Let me write down what I'm hearing: the add-on structure is creating friction with finance, Marchex is coming in lower per rooftop with scoring bundled, and that combination puts the renewal decision in question.

26
00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:49.417
Diego Alvarez: Am I missing anything?

27
00:03:50.084 --> 00:03:52.098
Brittany Sawyer: That's the shape of it.

28
00:03:53.326 --> 00:04:01.924
Frank DeLuca: One more thing, and this is smaller. The controller asked whether anything we're already paying for overlaps. I told her I'd ask.

29
00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:13.636
Diego Alvarez: I'll bring that to our team too, along with the invoice. I'm not going to improvise an answer on pricing on this call, that wouldn't help you.

30
00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:17.941
Frank DeLuca: Appreciated. I'd rather you come back with something real.

31
00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:22.758
Diego Alvarez: Who else needs to be in that conversation? Sounds like the controller.

32
00:04:23.194 --> 00:04:32.629
Frank DeLuca: Her name's Renata. She's the one with the spreadsheet. And if we get to the point of signing something, procurement gets a look.

33
00:04:33.359 --> 00:04:47.068
Diego Alvarez: Okay. Send me the invoice and I'll set up a follow-up for later this month, and I'll get Renata on it so she's hearing it directly instead of through both of you.

34
00:04:47.984 --> 00:04:51.491
Frank DeLuca: That works. Her Thursdays are usually open after two.

35
00:04:52.162 --> 00:04:58.051
Diego Alvarez: I'll send a couple of options. Anything else on your end before we wrap?

36
00:04:58.892 --> 00:05:08.535
Brittany Sawyer: We're onboarding two BDC reps the first week of November, so if there's anything they need on the reporting side, I'll ping you separately.

37
00:05:09.228 --> 00:05:13.699
Diego Alvarez: Please do. And tell the two sick ones I hope they're feeling better.

38
00:05:14.052 --> 00:05:20.081
Brittany Sawyer: They're back and they're fine, they just have a lot of catching up to do.

39
00:05:20.342 --> 00:05:24.393
Diego Alvarez: Alright, I'll get the follow-up on the calendar. Thanks Frank, thanks Brittany.

40
00:05:25.026 --> 00:05:25.827
Frank DeLuca: Thanks Diego.

41
00:05:26.142 --> 00:05:26.942
Brittany Sawyer: Talk soon.
